# Scope: libgit2-sys 0.18.5+1.9.4, AROS x86_64 ABIv11 only.
# Why: eza needs local repository status without an external Git executable.
# Use upstream non-mmap fallback and second-resolution stat; provide positioned
# I/O on the SDK, omit unavailable session/passwd lookups and reject networking.
# GIT_IO_SELECT is defined only to compile the ENOSYS p_poll stub: build.rs
# otherwise leaves no poll implementation and posix.c stops with #error.
# p_realpath uses Lock/NameFromLock: crt.library realpath() returned NULL,
# errno 2, even for "RAM:" and "SYS:C" (AROS One 1.3, pool v11-1,
# 2026-10-21), so repository open failed with "failed to resolve path".
# git_fs_path_owner_is reports the current user on AROS: volumes record no
# comparable owner and every repository was "not owned by current user".
# git_fs_path_to_dir adds no "/" after a volume colon: "Vol:/" is the
# parent of the root in AmigaDOS (review, 2026-10-21).
# A repository at a volume root (Vol:.git): the search from a file in it
# stopped at "Vol:" before looking for "Vol:.git" (ceiling one past the
# colon), and ignore/attribute files were read as "Vol:/.gitignore", which
# is the parent of the root (AROS One 1.3, pool v11-1, 2026-10-21). The
# ceiling is the colon, the walk ends when "Vol:" is its own parent, and no
# '/' follows a colon in attrcache.c, git_str_join3, the filesystem
# iterator root, git_fs_path_string_to_dir and the directory iterator
# (entries of "Vol:" were read as "Vol:/name": every status was D).
# Upstream status: local port adaptation; native repository coverage required.
# Verification: compiled by the libgit2-sys build script in the eza Cargo
# build (2026-10-21; the earlier 199-unit probe did not use build.rs features
# and missed the #error). Native results are in the port's validation docs.
